  "measures": [],
  "notes": "White light (the F, d and C lines, 486.1, 587.6 and 656.3 nm) through an equilateral N-SF11 prism turned to minimum deviation for the d line. Blue is bent most. Turn the prism a few degrees either way and watch the deviation pass through its minimum; swap the glass for N-BK7 to see how much less a crown glass disperses. The light is p polarised: at this angle of incidence, close to Brewster’s, hardly any is reflected at the faces; make it unpolarised to see the s light’s reflections."
